{
  "scope": "riscv-formal bounded model checks of the RVFI trace. Each check starts from reset and covers every input sequence up to its depth in cycles (formal/<config>.cfg); it is not an unbounded proof. Instruction words, load data, both ready signals and the interrupt lines are unconstrained. The extended core runs with RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, so M operations are checked as riscv-formal's alternative add/sub-and-xor operations: this verifies their decode, operand forwarding and hold logic, not the multiply/divide arithmetic, which tests/isa_compare.py compares with Spike. CSR instructions report no RVFI CSR ports, so the csrw and csr_ill checks do not run; the extended regression and the privilege suite cover CSR behavior.",
